                "caption": "Figure 1:Left:NAPE’s overview. The input spectrogram is split into patches and embedded into a sequence of embeddings. At each step, the model predicts the embedding of thenext patch(red border) using only the embeddings of thepreceding patches; patches atfuture positionsare hidden by the causal attention mask.Middle:The NAPE pipeline: patch embeddingszzare processed by the causal encoderhhand predictorggto produce predictionsz^\\hat{z}, which are compared against the targetszzunder stop-gradient using a similarity function𝒟\\mathcal{D}(i.e., negative cosine similarity).Right:Encoder architecture (hh): multiple stacked Transformer layers with pre-norm design, causal self-attention, LayerScale, and query-key normalization.",
